 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nSubquery unnesting optimization broken after recent changes\n\n#### Description\n\nThe subquery unnesting optimization is failing with an `IndexError: list index out of range` error. This appears to be affecting multiple optimization scenarios including correlated subqueries and complex query transformations.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\nfrom sqlglot import optimize\n\n# Example query that triggers the issue\nsql = \"\"\"\nSELECT *\nFROM table1 t1\nWHERE EXISTS (\n    SELECT 1\n    FROM table2 t2\n    WHERE t2.id = t1.id\n    AND t2.status = 'active'\n)\n\"\"\"\n\n# This should work but now raises IndexError\noptimized = optimize(sql, dialect=\"postgres\")\n```\n\nThe error occurs during the unnest_subqueries optimization step when processing correlated subqueries. The optimization process attempts to access list elements that are no longer available after recent code changes.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe query should be successfully optimized, potentially converting the EXISTS subquery to a JOIN or other equivalent form without raising any errors.\n\n#### Actual Behavior\n\n```\nIndexError: list index out of range\n```\n\nThis affects various types of subquery patterns and is breaking the optimization pipeline for queries that previously worked correctly.\n</issue>\n",
